    "faq": [
      {
        "q": "Why Choose Fiddler’s Roofing?",
        "a": "Fiddler’s Roofing is a Florida Certified Roofing Contractor, License CCC1333004, and has served Central Florida since 2003. We are also a GAF Master Elite® contractor for qualifying asphalt shingle roofs. Customers receive product-specific recommendations, available financing options, and a free estimate for the proposed work.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      },
      {
        "q": "How long does a metal roof last in Orlando?",
        "a": "Metal roofs are commonly chosen for long-term service, but a universal “40 to 80 years” promise is too broad for every system. Expected service life depends on the metal substrate, coating, profile, installation, exposure, maintenance, and repairs. We explain the product warranty and workmanship coverage for the specific roof being proposed.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      },
      {
        "q": "Can every metal roof withstand winds over 150 mph?",
        "a": "No. A blanket wind rating does not apply to every metal roof. Wind performance belongs to a tested roof assembly installed over a defined deck with specified fasteners and spacing. The correct question is whether the proposed assembly and installation meet the applicable requirements for the property.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      },
      {
        "q": "Will metal roofing lower my cooling costs?",
        "a": "A reflective metal finish may reduce roof-surface heat gain and cooling demand, especially in a warm climate. It does not guarantee a fixed percentage of savings. Color, solar reflectance, insulation, ventilation, HVAC efficiency, and building use all influence the result.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      },
      {
        "q": "Can a new metal roof reduce home insurance premiums?",
        "a": "It may help a home qualify for wind-mitigation credits when the roof covering and other documented features meet applicable requirements, but metal alone does not guarantee a discount. Ask your insurance carrier what documentation and inspection it requires before selecting a system.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      },
      {
        "q": "How much does metal roofing cost in Orlando?",
        "a": "The price depends on measured roof area, tear-off, deck repairs, roof complexity, access, selected system, steel gauge, finish, flashing, permits, and project details. A generic online range cannot accurately price a specific roof. For Orlando property owners, the reliable way to price the work is to schedule an inspection and receive a written estimate.",
        "source_url": "https://fiddlersroofing.com/"
      }
    ],
